Model <code>contactmethod/@value</code> Material quantities checked in the current body-contact configuration Non-smooth contact (NSC) <code>0</code> Restitution and resolved static/kinetic friction Smooth contact (SMC) <code>1</code> Restitution and resolved static/kinetic friction, plus Young's modulus and Poisson's ratio <p>The current numbered cases demonstrate both methods: <code>examples/chrono/07_DamBreakCubes/DamBreak1Cube_Def.xml</code> uses active NSC, and <code>examples/chrono/02_Spring/CaseInitialMotionSMC_Def.xml</code> uses active SMC. The latter is a separate two-block spring case; its material and body settings should not be mixed into the dam-break case.</p> <p>The following NSC configuration preserves the current dam-break body's name <code>cube1</code>, rather than the older slide's <code>cube</code>. The <code>_savedata</code> entry remains inactive.</p> <p>XML excerpt — collision-nsc. XML location: <code>case/execution/special</code>. Source: <code>examples/chrono/07_DamBreakCubes/DamBreak1Cube_Def.xml</code>.</p> <pre><code>&lt;chrono&gt;
    &lt;_savedata value="0.01" comment="Saves CSV with data exchange for each time interval (0=all steps)"/&gt;
    &lt;schemescale value="1" comment="Scale used to create the initial scheme of Chrono objects (default=1)"/&gt;
    &lt;collision activate="true"&gt;
        &lt;distancedp value="0.5" comment="Allowed collision overlap according Dp (default=0.5)"/&gt;
        &lt;contactmethod value="0" comment="Contact method type. 0:NSC (Non Smooth Contacts), 1:SMC (SMooth Contacts). (default=0)"/&gt;
    &lt;/collision&gt;
    &lt;bodyfloating id="cube1" mkbound="51" modelfile="AutoActual"/&gt;
    &lt;bodyfixed id="tank" mkbound="0" modelfile="AutoActual" modelnormal="invert"/&gt;
&lt;/chrono&gt;
</code></pre> <p>For comparison, this is the active collision element in the separate SMC spring case, under its own <code>chrono</code> parent:</p> <p>XML excerpt — collision-smc. XML location: <code>case/execution/special/chrono</code>. Source: <code>examples/chrono/02_Spring/CaseInitialMotionSMC_Def.xml</code>.</p> <pre><code>&lt;collision activate="true"&gt;
    &lt;distancedp value="0.5" comment="Allowed collision overlap according Dp (default=0.5)"/&gt;
    &lt;contactmethod value="1" comment="Contact method type. 0:NSC (Non Smooth Contacts), 1:SMC (SMooth Contacts). (default=0)"/&gt;
&lt;/collision&gt;
</code></pre> Item Meaning Units / condition <code>collision/@activate</code> Explicitly enables or disables Chrono contact modelling Boolean; supply the attribute when the element is present <code>distancedp/@value</code> Allowed overlap expressed as a multiple of particle spacing <code>dp</code> Dimensionless; <code>0.5</code> corresponds to <code>0.5 dp</code> <code>contactmethod/@value</code> Chooses NSC or SMC <code>0</code> or <code>1</code> <code>modelfile</code> Geometry associated with a body for contact modelling File or supported automatic-generation selector <code>modelnormal</code> Orientation of collision-model normals <code>original</code>, <code>invert</code> or <code>twoface</code> in the current reader <p>Use <code>activate="false"</code> to disable the collision section explicitly. A method value inside a disabled section is not evidence of active contact modelling. The XML reader requires <code>activate</code> when a <code>collision</code> element is present.</p>

Element within <code>phase</code> Documented meaning Context <code>rhop</code> Density of the phase The reference and cases use <code>rhop</code> <code>csound</code> Phase speed of sound, m/s Optional; otherwise the value calculated by GenCase is used <code>gamma</code> Polytropic index in the equation of state Optional; otherwise the value in <code>constantsdef</code> is used <code>phasetype</code> Phase-model selector The documented historical module provides value 0 <p>The module description uses the phase-specific sound speed when obtaining pressure from the equation of state, but uses the maximum sound speed across the phases in the CFL time-step restriction. Specifying a smaller sound speed for one phase therefore does not remove the restriction imposed by a faster phase.</p> <p>XML excerpt — phase-eos-properties. Historical module context; XML location: <code>case/execution/special/nnphases/phase</code>. Source: <code>doc/xml_format/_FmtXML_MphaseNNewtonian.xml</code>.</p> <pre><code>&lt;rhop value="1000" comment="Density of the phase" /&gt;
&lt;csound value="80" comment="Speed of sound for phase (m/s)" /&gt;
&lt;gamma value="7" comment="Gamma polytropic index value for phase" /&gt;
</code></pre> <p>These are property elements inside a phase, not separate execution parameters. The original module description does not recommend density ratios greater than two. This recommendation belongs to that formulation and should not be interpreted as a general limit for every multiphase method or software release. The supplied documentation does not establish an interface reconstruction scheme, a mixture law or a general maximum phase count.</p>
